1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,407
The numbers were brand new and, yeah, they also seemed to contradict each other.

2
00:00:05,407 --> 00:00:13,845
A councilor praised the rise in enrolment; a pensioner in the same queue said the buses had not improved at all.

3
00:00:13,845 --> 00:00:23,307
“Your figures are convincing,” Professor Zhao said, “but they cannot describe what a commuter feels when the bus never comes.

4
00:00:23,307 --> 00:00:27,461
You ought to ask what the numbers hide.”

5
00:00:27,461 --> 00:00:30,396
The team listed what they lacked.

6
00:00:30,396 --> 00:00:37,424
A single, vivid story is not enough; a hundred forgettable ones are not either.

7
00:00:37,424 --> 00:00:42,827
The complexity was real, and the schedule was merely tolerable.

8
00:00:42,827 --> 00:00:50,840
“The data vary by street,” Lin said, “and a smelly corridor can be more harmful than a missing sign.

9
00:00:50,840 --> 00:01:08,646
The corridor is virtually empty after eight, but the bus is incredibly slow all day.” A naughty child had once kicked the bag of a bully down the stairs; the incident was attributable to a broken lift, not to a bad temper.

10
00:01:08,646 --> 00:01:12,570
Being truly independent was harder than it looked.

11
00:01:12,570 --> 00:01:20,847
A talented student could enhance one section, but a diverse team needed the flexibility to rewrite the rest.

12
00:01:20,847 --> 00:01:26,136
Accordingly, they invited a pensioner's group to check the route.

13
00:01:26,136 --> 00:01:31,165
“I shiver when I think of the old plan,” a comrade said.

14
00:01:31,165 --> 00:01:40,892
“It was predictable and useless.” There was a vacancy on the committee, and filling it would complicate everything.

15
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:45,391
The opponent of the project was not a person but a habit.

16
00:01:45,391 --> 00:01:57,128
A raging argument about an addictive game, a rumour about brutality in the dormitory, and an elective course on manners all drifted through the same group chat.

17
00:01:57,128 --> 00:02:02,492
Lin found it hurtful and, at first, unbelievable.

18
00:02:02,492 --> 00:02:06,546
“Am I nosy?” Maya asked.

19
00:02:06,546 --> 00:02:09,095
“No,” he said.

20
00:02:09,095 --> 00:02:13,465
“You are hopeful, and that is rare.”

21
00:02:13,465 --> 00:02:23,622
They agreed to improve the report, to enrol two more volunteers, and to enrich the sample with voices a spreadsheet cannot hold.

22
00:02:23,622 --> 00:02:30,265
The work was not glamorous; it was merely useful, though the queue was long.

23
00:02:30,265 --> 00:02:49,760
“Yeah,” Maya said, “a leader is someone who asks again.” She had grown used to the smelly corridor and the lady with the umbrella, and so had the president of the student union, who now stood beside them at the gate with wet hair and a personal note in his hand.

24
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:54,579
Three months ago the same man had called the plan forgettable.

25
00:02:54,579 --> 00:02:59,868
“Good lord,” he said, “you have achieved something small.

26
00:02:59,868 --> 00:03:05,501
My major taught me to develop a model; you taught me to visit one.

27
00:03:05,501 --> 00:03:14,183
Give me the list.” The university press wanted a photograph for its college edition.
